   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 📡 Time-Series Anomaly Detection in Air Quality Sensor Data\n",
    "### Inspired by SIATA / NASA AERONET atmospheric monitoring networks\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Business Context\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Why does this matter for industry?**  \n",
    "> Anomaly detection in time series is one of the most requested skills in data science roles  \n",
    "> across manufacturing, fintech, e-commerce, and IoT. The exact same pipeline applies to:\n",
    "> - **Manufacturing:** Detecting faulty sensors or production anomalies in real time\n",
    "> - **Finance:** Identifying unusual transaction patterns (fraud detection)\n",
    "> - **Retail:** Spotting abnormal drops or spikes in daily sales\n",
    "> - **Infrastructure:** Predictive maintenance of industrial equipment\n",
    "\n",
    "**Analogies:**\n",
    "| Environmental Monitoring | Industry |\n",
    "|--------------------------|----------|\n",
    "| PM2.5 sensor readings | Sales/revenue daily data |\n",
    "| Sensor failure (reading = 0) | System outage / missing data |\n",
    "| Pollution spike event | Fraud transaction / demand surge |\n",
    "| Daily cycle pattern | Intraday seasonality in transactions |\n",
    "| Wind/temp covariates | External factors (holidays, campaigns) |\n",
    "| Station network | Branch / store network |\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Dataset Description\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Source:** Synthetic time series modeled on SIATA (Sistema de Alerta Temprana de Medellín)  \n",
    "  and NASA AERONET atmospheric monitoring data\n",
    "- **Period:** 2 years of hourly data (Jan 2022 – Dec 2023), 17,520 observations\n",
    "- **Anomaly types injected:**\n",
    "  - **Spikes:** Sudden PM2.5 surges (equipment malfunction, pollution episodes) — 25 events\n",
    "  - **Flatlines:** Sensor offline / reading = 0 — 15 events\n",
    "  - **Total anomalies:** ~285 hours (~1.6% of data)\n",
    "\n",
    "| Column | Description | Business Analog |\n",
    "|--------|-------------|----------------|\n",
    "| `timestamp` | Hourly datetime | Transaction timestamp |\n",
    "| `pm25_ugm3` | PM2.5 concentration (µg/m³) | KPI value |\n",
    "| `temperature_c` | Temperature (°C) | External covariate |\n",
    "| `humidity_pct` | Relative humidity (%) | External covariate |\n",
    "| `wind_speed_ms` | Wind speed (m/s) | External covariate |\n",
    "| `is_anomaly` | Ground truth label (0/1) | **Fraud/anomaly flag** |"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 0. Environment Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import matplotlib.dates as mdates\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from scipy import stats\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import IsolationForest\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (classification_report, confusion_matrix,\n",
    "                              f1_score, precision_recall_curve,\n",
    "                              average_precision_score, ConfusionMatrixDisplay)\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.rcParams.update({\n",
    "    'figure.dpi': 130,\n",
    "    'axes.spines.top': False,\n",
    "    'axes.spines.right': False,\n",
    "})\n",
    "BLUE  = '#1f4e79'\n",
    "RED   = '#c55a11'\n",
    "LIGHT = '#9dc3e6'\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Libraries loaded ✓')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Data Loading & Parsing"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df = pd.read_csv('../data/air_quality_timeseries.csv', parse_dates=['timestamp'])\n",
    "df = df.set_index('timestamp').sort_index()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Shape:  {df.shape[0]:,} rows × {df.shape[1]} columns')\n",
    "print(f'Period: {df.index.min().date()} → {df.index.max().date()}')\n",
    "print(f'Missing values: {df.isna().sum().sum()}')\n",
    "print(f'Anomalies in ground truth: {df[\"is_anomaly\"].sum()} ({df[\"is_anomaly\"].mean()*100:.1f}%)')\n",
    "df.head(4)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
